{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-watch-app-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-1","surface":"watch","area":"watch/app","refs":["F-watch-103","F-watch-106","F-watch-109"],"severity":"S3","title":"A rest started by logging a set on the watch ignores 'Ring through Do Not Disturb'","what":"When a set is logged on the watch, the watch starts the rest itself at once. It takes the 'Ring through Do Not Disturb' choice from the last rest it stored, but that stored choice is wiped every time a rest ends. So the watch's own rest always ends with an ordinary buzz that Do Not Disturb holds back. Usually the phone's own rest arrives a moment later and replaces it, but when the phone does not take the set ('Not saved', phone out of reach) the member with the switch on gets no buzz through Do Not Disturb.","expected":"With 'Ring through Do Not Disturb' on, every end-of-rest buzz on the watch gets through Do Not Disturb, including a rest the watch started itself.","evidence":["apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:210-219","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:350-358","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:387-401","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/MainActivity.kt:445-460","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:207-229","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:245"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"dnd-choice-wiped-after-each-rest","who":"members who log sets on the watch with Ring through Do Not Disturb on","how_often":"each watch-logged set the phone does not take","fix_line":"Keep the Do Not Disturb choice on the watch apart from the rest, so a rest the watch starts uses it too","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-watch-app-02","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-1","surface":"watch","area":"watch/app","refs":["F-watch-122","F-watch-120"],"severity":"S3","title":"Once the watch has seen MettleUp on the phone, it never again says the phone app is missing","what":"The watch remembers for good that the phone once had MettleUp. If the member later removes MettleUp from the phone, the watch's check finds no app but the remembered 'seen' wins, so 'Get MettleUp on your phone' never shows again. The member sees 'Start a workout on your phone', which cannot work.","expected":"When the connected phone no longer has MettleUp, the watch shows 'Get MettleUp on your phone' with its Play Store button again.","evidence":["apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchLayout.kt:109-111","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:409-413","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/MainActivity.kt:843-854","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchSync.kt:23-24"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"phone-app-seen-never-reset","who":"members who remove the phone app but keep the watch app","how_often":"rarely","fix_line":"Let a current phone app's missing sign clear the remembered 'seen', keeping it only for old phone apps that send no sign","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
